Portions of the platform audio-capture and power layers are adapted from
anarlog. The adaptation is substantial rather than verbatim: anarlog's capture
is asynchronous and `Stream`-based over its own internal workspace crates,
while this project's `capture::source::AudioSource` is synchronous and
pull-based, so the device setup, format negotiation and sample-conversion logic
was reworked to drain through a ring buffer instead.

Files in this repository containing adapted code, each also carrying an
in-file attribution comment:

  src-tauri/platform/src/windows/speaker.rs   <- crates/audio-actual/src/speaker/windows.rs
  src-tauri/platform/src/windows/power.rs     <- crates/power/src/windows.rs
  src-tauri/platform/src/macos/speaker.rs     <- crates/audio-actual/src/speaker/macos.rs
  src-tauri/platform/src/macos/power.rs       <- crates/power/src/macos.rs
  src-tauri/platform/src/mic.rs               <- crates/audio-actual/src/mic.rs
  src-tauri/platform/src/ring.rs              <- crates/audio-actual/src/rt_ring.rs

